This equation, $T^{\mu
u} = T^{
u\mu}$, asserts that the stress-energy-momentum tensor is a symmetric rank-2 tensor, meaning its components are unchanged upon the interchange of its indices.

symmetry-of-stress-energy-tensor-d4c6bb6.limits_and_boundary:
The symmetry $T^{\mu
u} = T^{
u\mu}$ is a foundational property that holds in all regimes where standard general relativity and classical field theory are valid. It is not an approximation and does not depend on limits like $v \to c$ or $\hbar \to 0$. However, in theories that incorporate intrinsic spin, such as Einstein-Cartan theory, the stress-energy tensor is not symmetric, and its antisymmetric part is related to the spin tensor.
